<h1>Leah Cunningham Pouw</h1>
<p>45th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.leah45.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (leah45.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Second declared challenger to Ald. Jim Gardiner, saying she sees a disconnect between the ward&#39;s communities. She is running on revitalizing business corridors, easing traffic congestion and making roads safe for all users, reducing flooding and fixing potholes faster, an open and responsive ward office, and a city budget that does not balance the books on the backs of everyday Chicagoans.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Policy researcher at the University of Illinois School of Social Work with a Master of Public Policy from the University of Chicago; two terms as secretary of both the Wildwood Local School Council and the Wildwood Park Advisory Council.</p>
